@startuml
title CQRS Data Flow - Add an aircraft, then read it (aircraft-service)

autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Client\n(Postman)" as Client
participant "HAProxy\nPC1 :443" as HAP
participant "API Gateway\n(1 of 2)" as GW
participant "aircraft-service\ninstance A" as A
participant "aircraft-service\ninstance B" as B
database "PostgreSQL\naircraft_db (PC5)" as PG
queue "RabbitMQ\naircraft.exchange\n-> aircraft.sync.queue" as MQ
database "Redis cluster\nredis-aircraft-1..3" as RD

== Command (write side) ==
Client -> HAP : POST /api/hangar/aircraft\nBearer JWT
HAP -> GW : TCP pass-through (round robin)
GW -> A : lb://aircraft-service\n+ X-Gateway-Secret
A -> PG : load AircraftModel
A -> PG : save Aircraft
A -> MQ : publish AircraftSyncEvent\nkey aircraft.event.created
A --> Client : 201 Created

== Projection (asynchronous) ==
MQ -> B : deliver to one consumer\n(competing consumers on the same queue)
B -> RD : save AircraftRedis\nhash Aircraft:<registration>

== Query (read side) ==
Client -> HAP : GET /api/hangar/aircraft/{reg}
HAP -> GW
GW -> A : lb://aircraft-service
A -> RD : findById(reg)
A --> Client : 200 OK (AircraftRedis)

note over PG, RD
  Reads never touch PostgreSQL.
  The read side is eventually consistent: a GET sent
  right after the POST can still miss the new aircraft.
end note

@enduml
